// CROWN — latency rides a constructor payload whose fn type is DECLARED on
// the type (`type Box = Box(() -> Int)`), not quantified. Matched out and
// called under `with !E`. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// The quantified payload (leak-variant-latent) refuses; this one checked
// clean and ran at 7 through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23), because
// the declared payload row is ONE identity cell on the constructor's scheme:
// construction writes an instantiated copy, the match reads another copy of
// a cell nothing writes. Hβ.effects.variant-payload-fn-row.
effect E { op() -> Int }
type Box = Box(() -> Int)
fn loud() = op()
fn bad() with !E = match Box(loud) {
  Box(f) => f(),
}
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = bad() ~> h
